#
# Regenerates package-lock.json and remote/package-lock.json after the
# Copilot-removal patches drop dependencies (ADR 0002 decision 6: lockfiles are
# regenerated by script, never hand-edited; docs/design/axis-shell-stage1.md section 2.8).
#
# Runs `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts` in . and remote/
# (upstream's own precedent; install scripts never run) with the npm bundled
# with the pinned Node (exactly NPM_VERSION below), then asserts:
#   - the removed entries are exactly the EXPECTED_* lists below (name@version);
#   - no entry was added, and every kept entry is unchanged (all fields,
#     including version, resolved and integrity);
#   - the root entry lost only the agent SDK names from its dependencies;
#   - zod is still a direct dependency, resolved at top-level node_modules/zod,
#     at the same version (threat model SC-3 check 4, ADR 0003 D2);
#   - each regenerated lockfile has the sha256 recorded below.
# Every removed entry is printed so the sync PR can review it. At an upstream
# sync, update the lists and hashes from the printed output after review.
#
# Network: the npm registry, for package metadata only.
set -euo pipefail

NPM_VERSION=11.19.1
SHA256_ROOT=15a0ae34a74ab0b932fec76dd9583de331731eded72dbe44a8be35902eb559af
SHA256_REMOTE=1b2fb6683b474e96b3e230afd3a0d5298c9592ed35e343303a741446599ec30f
ROOT_SDK_NAMES='@anthropic-ai/sdk @github/copilot-sdk @vscode/copilot-api @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk @openai/codex'

EXPECTED_ROOT='
node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk@0.3.304
node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk-darwin-arm64@0.3.304
node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk-darwin-x64@0.3.304
